#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281285 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129205 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb891682-26ae-541c-a92d-a79756d1714e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Solid Given in Set Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b3410aa-3741-574c-a561-ca42745d30c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "39" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278698} {:answer/id #uuid "27773d7f-25a8-52fe-bf01-68d9f7772331" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{33}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278943} {:answer/id #uuid "355cd015-3c29-5af2-b4f6-238cf9b24f2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279057} {:answer/id #uuid "4bc0b319-2b34-5da0-9a70-f1965d979755" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{32}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279268} {:answer/id #uuid "51b7c11f-8dbf-5b54-9513-c9741d294524" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279336}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b3410aa-3741-574c-a561-ca42745d30c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "39" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278698} :answer-field/id #uuid "862cee1d-edf0-59fb-96ad-6bf304ab07ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281077}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "edd7e04c-fb5f-5755-adfd-ac7811c6b1ad" :question/math-academy-id "q-161653" :question/problem "Find the volume of the solid $R$ given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,1\\le y\\le 4,\\,2\\le z\\le 3y+x}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that we have a three-dimensional type I region.\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{2}^{3y+x}\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{4}[z]_{z=2}^{z=3y+x}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{4}3y+x-2\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{2}+xy-2y]}_{y=1}^{y=4}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,[(24+4x-8)-(\\frac{3}{2}+x-2)]\\,dx \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{2}3x+\\frac{33}{2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={[\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{33}{2}x]}_{x=0}^{x=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(2)^{2}}{2}+\\frac{33}{2}(2)-0 \\\\  & =39.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412201 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129205 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb891682-26ae-541c-a92d-a79756d1714e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Solid Given in Set Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ec6ec01-733e-5f02-af23-9cc8caaac3a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412118} {:answer/id #uuid "7908b9c9-85f1-5fb7-8993-c1b1c1be6014" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412124} {:answer/id #uuid "b9a79b99-32b0-5d67-90f5-be49d7031cdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412146} {:answer/id #uuid "bc206240-eb24-501d-9e9e-fc7fd50a7902" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412147} {:answer/id #uuid "d8ffd103-8f74-5398-842a-0cf2cb86197a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412160}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc206240-eb24-501d-9e9e-fc7fd50a7902" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412147} :answer-field/id #uuid "3acdc6ec-2a12-547a-88f2-73cc8411f0a8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412179}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "89162549-49ec-507f-b56c-dea9e66a6c30" :question/math-academy-id "q-161654" :question/problem "Find the volume of the solid $R$ given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,1-x\\le y\\le 1+x,\\,0\\le z\\le xy}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that we have a three-dimensional type I region.\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-x}^{1+x}{\\int }_{0}^{xy}\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-x}^{1+x}[z]_{z=0}^{z=xy}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-x}^{1+x}xy\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y=1-x}^{y=1+x}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{x}{2}((1+x)^{2}-(1-x)^{2})\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{x}{2}((1+2x+{x}^{2})-(1-2x+{x}^{2}))\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{x}{2}(4x)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2{x}^{2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={[\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281299 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129206 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "43198aae-a4dd-5b79-803a-1bb625a96355" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Solid Given a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15ae8429-f69d-5ace-9302-7610fc9d936c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278786} {:answer/id #uuid "558b62f0-5307-5c8d-b221-d64f4a347db2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279373} {:answer/id #uuid "67bcdefa-ae0f-563d-a606-0b4fc3264810" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279535} {:answer/id #uuid "b3dac8f5-8001-5b88-b8f5-8efb16420750" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280176} {:answer/id #uuid "f2dd39da-a465-5001-a8a3-a1dadc0b4509" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280709}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15ae8429-f69d-5ace-9302-7610fc9d936c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278786} :answer-field/id #uuid "95e414d6-af68-52cc-a7c3-68806836a587" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281103}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1e6adf41-eeec-5787-910a-9b879a193cb7" :question/math-academy-id "q-161695" :question/problem "![](images/21/214d629cdac48642a7a8b4d435f91098388a7a799bd7e70d5b7c91ae028714c3.png)\n\nFind the volume of the solid region above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the top one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" :question/worked-solution "![](images/bf/bf9c4790a8e31e000d2aeb7f7e557661683d3f52d737ba1b99abd407c15d6e99.png)\n\n  \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type I region\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,y)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 3+x-y},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 2}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $xy$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](images/74/74954715928551ebb271cdfd461d783778b02b7944cbfd5502d6d06011408ad8.png)\n\nHence, the type I representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 3+x-y}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3+x-y}dz\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[z]_{z=0}^{z=3+x-y}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(3+x-y)-0\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}3+x-y\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[(3+x)y-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}((3+x)(2)-\\frac{{2}^{2}}{2})-0\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}4+2x\\,dx \\\\  & =[4x+{x}^{2}]_{x=0}^{x=2} \\\\  & =(8+4)-0 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
